    "sources": [],
    "summary": "Overnight, cross-asset tone was mixed but orderly: the S&P 500 closed near 7201, the Nasdaq at 23586, and the VIX at 26.36, with equities holding up while implied volatility stayed elevated. WTI settled at 83.68 and Brent at 94.61; gold was firm at 3535.80 and copper at 5.33, apart from earlier bearish metals sentiment in the tape. FX showed modest dollar give-back versus EURUSD at 1.0975 (+0.37% on the day) and AUDUSD at 0.6635 (+1%), while USDJPY sat near 159.26. U.S. yields eased over the week, with the 10-year at 4.85% (\u221222bp over five days), even as December Fed meeting pricing built roughly 44bp of cumulative tightening to a post-meeting rate near 4.31%. Euro-area 10-year yields rose 4bp to 3.29% on the latest observation."
